<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; The Incarnation" cic="CCC 484-511" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What does the phrase &laquo;The Word became flesh&raquo; (Jn 1:14) mean?</li>
<li>What are the four reasons the Word became flesh, according to the Catechism?</li>
<li>What did Mary answer the angel Gabriel at the Annunciation?</li>
<li>What does it mean that Jesus is true God and true man?</li>
<li>What does the title <em>Theotokos</em> that the Church gives to Mary mean?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. What does it mean to you that God chose to become a human body, with all its limitations?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think about how vulnerable a baby is: totally dependent on others to survive. God chose to start that way. What does that tell you about how God relates to us?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Mary said &laquo;yes&raquo; without knowing everything that would come after. Is there a &laquo;yes&raquo; God is asking of you today that you are afraid to give?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">It could be a big or small decision. Write about that situation and, next to it, what you would need to be able to say &laquo;let it be done&raquo; like Mary.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. If Jesus is truly man and experienced weariness, hunger, sadness, and temptation, how does that change how you see your own sufferings?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Does it help you feel understood? Give you hope? Or is it hard to believe that God really understands what it means to be human?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. &laquo;God became man so that man might become God.&raquo; What do you think this phrase means for your daily life?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">How would your day-to-day life change if you truly lived convinced that you are called to share in God&rsquo;s life?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. Mary is a model of faith. Which quality of Mary would you like to imitate in your relationship with God?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Her availability? Her courage? Her silence? Her trust? Write why you would like to have that quality.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Meditate on Mary&rsquo;s &laquo;Let it be done&raquo;</h4>
<p>Sit in a quiet place. Imagine the scene of the Annunciation: the room, the light, the angel, Mary. Listen to the angel&rsquo;s words. Now imagine those words are also for you: &laquo;Do not be afraid... the Lord is with you.&raquo; What is God saying to you today? Write a brief letter of response, beginning with &laquo;Let it be done to me according to your word.&raquo;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. Read Philippians 2:6-11 &mdash; The hymn of the Incarnation</h4>
<p>Paul wrote one of the most beautiful texts in the New Testament about Christ&rsquo;s self-emptying. Read it aloud. Underline the words that describe what Christ gave up (his divine condition) and those that describe what he took on (the condition of a servant). Write a three-line reflection on what strikes you most in this text.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Look up an image of the Annunciation</h4>
<p>Search online for Fra Angelico&rsquo;s &laquo;Annunciation&raquo; or Leonardo da Vinci&rsquo;s. Observe it in silence for 5 minutes. Notice the details: the colors, the postures, the expressions, the light. What does this image tell you about the mystery of the Incarnation? Write your impressions.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;And the Word became flesh and dwelt among us, and we have seen his glory, glory as of the only Son from the Father, full of grace and truth&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; John 1:14</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Lord Jesus Christ, Son of God made man,<br />
thank you for choosing to share our flesh.<br />
You were not ashamed to become like us,<br />
to weep our tears, to bear our wounds.<br />
Teach me to receive you as Mary received you:<br />
with an open heart, without reserve, without fear.<br />
May your will be done in me,<br />
today and always.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

